Continuation of Phase 1. This PRD builds on AI Grader — New Result Experience (Phase 1). The student result screen (cover page, annotations, tabs, download, report, rating) is exactly the same as Phase 1 for every test type. Phase 2 adds (1) multi-question hybrid subjective tests and (2) a reviewer toolkit on SEP so that everything the student sees in the result can be edited by the reviewer.

Glossary and Full Forms

General terms

SEP: Student Evaluation Portal / Teacher Evaluation Portal. The web portal where copies are allotted, evaluated and reviewed. Link

Hybrid test: a test evaluated by AI + reviewer. AI evaluates first, then a reviewer reviews and corrects the evaluation on SEP before the student sees the result.

Pure AI test: a test evaluated by AI only, with no reviewer. This is the Phase 1 scope.

Online test: the student attempts in the app or web, writes the answers on their own paper and uploads them.

Offline test: the student writes the physical copy, and the Batch Manager uploads the scanned copy through admin.

BM: Batch Manager. Uploads offline copies through admin.

Toolkit: the set of tools on SEP that the reviewer uses to add, edit, move, resize, change or remove elements on the student's copy (Section 8).

New Result Experience: the annotated student result screen built in Phase 1.

Roles on SEP

SEP has three roles:

Admin: allots copies to evaluators and reviewers.

Evaluator: evaluates a copy for the first time.

Reviewer: reviews an evaluated copy and corrects it. In Hybrid tests the AI evaluation is reviewed by the reviewer, and this PRD refers to the person using the toolkit as the reviewer.

Types of annotations

The student's answer copy carries two types of annotations, as defined in Phase 1 (§4.4). Both types are fully editable on SEP in Phase 2.

Type 1: Highlighted bounding box. A numbered, coloured box drawn around a part of the answer. Every box has a feedback comment with the same number and colour. A box without feedback is not allowed. Colours: red = mistake, yellow = needs improvement, green = correct.

Type 2: Handwritten teacher-style marks. Marks drawn like a teacher marking with a pen. They have no numbered box and no feedback comment. The Type 2 marks are: tick, cross, underline, strike-through, circled score and text stamp. Only the underline can optionally carry a short comment.

1. Introduction

1.1 Context

AI Grader evaluates handwritten answer sheets and assigns marks. In Hybrid tests the evaluation is done by AI first and then reviewed by a human reviewer on SEP before the student sees the result. Hybrid subjective tests run in two modes, and volume is split roughly evenly between them, so both must be supported together:

Online – the student attempts through PW app/any platform, writes on their own paper and uploads it through pw app/any platform.

Offline – the physical copy is collected offline and uploaded by the Batch Manager (BM) through admin.

Phase 1 shipped the New Result Experience for Pure AI tests (online, in-app). Phase 1 §7.1 already commits Phase 2 to Subjective/Hybrid tests, online + offline, all platforms, with SEP edits reflecting in the student result. This document details that scope.

