1.3 Problem

No multi-question tests. A hybrid subjective test can have only one question. Multi-question tests cannot be run, in either online or offline mode.

SEP cannot edit the new result. The Phase 1 result has numbered highlight boxes, handwritten-style marks, stamps and a question-wise marks table. Reviewers need to be able to correct all of it, otherwise reviewed tests cannot use the New Result Experience.

Design and tech need one clear definition of what is editable, how, and with what rules.

2. Objectives

Primary: Make the New Result Experience live for all subjective tests (Hybrid/Pure AI, single and multi-question, online and offline, Web/Android/iOS), with every reviewer change on SEP reflected in the student's result.

Enable students to attempt multi-question subjective tests online.

Enable BMs to upload copies of multi-question tests offline using the same admin flow.

Give reviewers a toolkit on SEP to add, edit, move, resize, change and remove every annotation element, marks and feedback on the student copy.

Keep the student result identical to Phase 1 so there is one result experience to build, test and support.

3. Scope

In scope

Hybrid subjective tests, single and multi-question

Online (student upload) and Offline (BM upload) flows

Web, Android, iOS for the student side

Copy quality check for multi-question uploads

SEP reviewer toolkit and edit rules for every Phase 1 result element

Student result in the Phase 1 New Result Experience, reflecting the reviewed version

What does not change: single-question hybrid tests keep working as today; offline BM upload entry point stays the same; AI evaluation, the reviewer and the student report flow work as they do today; the Phase 1 result screen and student-side controls (Hide/Show Feedback, Download, Report, Rating) stay the same.

4. Proposed Solution

Channels: Web, Android, iOS (student). Admin (BM upload). SEP (reviewer, web only).

Upload, submission, evaluation and result are all test-wise. The student uploads the complete answer copy once, as a PDF or as images, submits the whole test once, and gets one result.

Quality check after the upload on the copy (readable, handwritten, has evaluatable content). Only the question where the check finds an issue is sent back for re-upload, and only once. After that the student can still submit.

Offline stays one complete scanned copy pdf per student, uploaded by the BM.

Same evaluation pipeline for online and offline: AI evaluates → copy goes to SEP → reviewer reviews with the toolkit → final reviewed copy goes to the student.

Student only ever sees the reviewed version, never the AI draft.

SEP toolkit: every element in the Phase 1 result is editable using a set of tools (Section 8).

5. User Flows

5.1 Student journey: online multi-question test

The student opens All Tests → Subjective tab and selects the test.

The student sees all questions of the test in one scrolling list, with the timer and test details at the top and the Upload Answers button at the bottom.

The student reads the questions and writes the answers on their own paper.

The student taps Upload Answers and uploads the complete answer copy once, as a PDF or as images.

The quality check runs on the copy. If a question has an issue, the student is asked to re-upload the answer for that question, one time only.

The student submits the full test.

The student waits while AI evaluates and the reviewer reviews, and sees the evaluation-in-progress state.

The student opens the result in the New Result Experience.

