7. SEP Reviewer Toolkit

Principle: whatever the student sees in the Phase 1 result is editable by the reviewer on SEP. The reviewer works on the same view the student will get, with a toolkit to change it. The reviewer's final version is what the student sees.

7.1 What is editable (element by element)

Result element (Phase 1)

Reviewer can

Rules

Cover page: student details (name, course, class, board, test name, contact no., test date)

View only

System data. Fields shown per cohort as in Phase 1 §4.3.

Cover page: question-wise marks table

Edit Marks obtained per question

Max marks are read-only. Marks cannot be below 0 or above the question's max marks. Decimals allowed. Unattempted question shows 0.

Cover page: Marks obtained / Total marks

Not edited directly

Auto-calculated: obtained = sum of question marks; total = sum of max marks (Phase 1 §4.3 D).

Cover page: Remark

Not edited directly

Auto-derived from marks % with the Phase 1 logic and cohort configuration. Re-derived whenever marks change.

Parameter-wise marks table (UPSC only)

Edit

Reviewers can edit parameter-level marks on SEP.

Overall summary / feedback page (UPSC only)

Edit the text

Free text. Cannot be saved empty if the cohort shows this page.

